Subject: [PATCH] t2bce_ave: certify idle state for hibernation rebuild

The AVE client allocates BCE queues only inside an active encoding session.
Its existing PM prepare callback tears that session down, destroys all four
queue pairs and frees their DMA rings before the BCE core requests
SLEEP_NO_STATE.

Register explicit no-state drop and rebuild callbacks so the core can
distinguish this prepared queue-free client from an unsupported client.  The
callbacks deliberately do no work: queue destruction belongs to the earlier
session teardown, and userspace must restart streaming after resume.

This is an offline follow-up to the BCE queue-reconstruction candidate.  It
does not preserve an active encoding session across hibernation and has not
been installed or hardware-qualified.

---
diff --git a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_ave/ave.c b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_ave/ave.c
--- a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_ave/ave.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_ave/ave.c
@@ -38,9 +38,24 @@ static int t2bce_ave_pm_prepare(void *userdata)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void t2bce_ave_pm_drop_no_state_queues(void *userdata)
+{
+	/* pm_prepare has already torn down the only AVE queue owner. */
+	(void)userdata;
+}
+
+static int t2bce_ave_pm_rebuild_no_state_queues(void *userdata)
+{
+	/* Userspace must create a new encoding session after resume. */
+	(void)userdata;
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct t2bce_core_client_pm_ops t2bce_ave_pm_ops = {
 	.shutdown = t2bce_ave_shutdown,
 	.pm_prepare = t2bce_ave_pm_prepare,
+	.pm_drop_no_state_queues = t2bce_ave_pm_drop_no_state_queues,
+	.pm_rebuild_no_state_queues = t2bce_ave_pm_rebuild_no_state_queues,
 };
 
 static int __init t2bce_ave_init(void)
